{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>Zebulun, at the shore of seas.</b> He mentioned the tribes in the order of their births; only Zebulun he mentioned before Issachar, because the inheritance of Issachar fell between Zebulun and Dan. Another interpretation: because Zebulun engaged in trade on behalf of Issachar, therefore he placed Zebulun first." "<b>By Sidon.</b> For it is a place of commerce, as it is written: ״סוחר צידון עובר ים מלאוך״ (a merchant of Sidon passing over the sea fills you), and therefore Moses blessed him: ״שמח זבולן בצאתך״ (rejoice, Zebulun, in your going out) — to trade." "<b>By Sidon.</b> Adjacent to Sidon, like ״וסכות על הארן״ (and you shall make booths over the Ark)."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 49, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:09:12.230573954Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}